.TH UNPACKROM 1 "October 11, 2026" "Vircon32 DevTools 26.04.24" "Vircon32 Development Tools"
.SH NAME
unpackrom \- extract the program, textures and sounds from a Vircon32 ROM
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unpackrom
.RB [ \-v ]
.I rom.v32
.I output\-folder
.br
.B unpackrom
.B \-\-help
.br
.B unpackrom
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unpackrom
does the opposite of
.BR packrom (1):
it takes a Vircon32 cartridge or BIOS file apart, writing everything it
contains into
.IR output\-folder ,
which is created if it does not exist (an existing file of that name is
an error). For a ROM file named
.IR game.v32 ,
it writes:
.TP
.I game.vbin
The program, as a VBIN binary (see
.BR disassemble (1)).
.TP
.IR textures/texture0.vtex ", " textures/texture1.vtex ", ..."
The textures, in id order (see
.BR vircon2png (1)).
.TP
.IR sounds/sound0.vsnd ", " sounds/sound1.vsnd ", ..."
The sounds, in id order (see
.BR vircon2wav (1)).
.TP
.I game.xml
A ROM definition listing all of the above, with the original title,
type and versions, from which
.BR packrom (1)
rebuilds the same ROM.
.TP
.IR Make.sh ", " Make.bat
Build scripts (shell and Windows batch) that run
.B packrom
on the definition, writing
.IR bin/game.v32 .
.I Make.sh
is written without execute permission; run it as
.BR "bash Make.sh" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose: report each step.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and author, and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The ROM was unpacked.
.TP
.B 1
Any error, printed as
.IR "unpackrom: error: description" .
.SH EXAMPLES
Unpack a cartridge, convert its assets to editable files, and turn its
program back into assembly:
.PP
.RS
.nf
unpackrom game.v32 game\-unpacked
cd game\-unpacked
vircon2png textures/texture0.vtex
vircon2wav sounds/sound0.vsnd
disassemble game.vbin \-o game.asm
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR packrom (1),
.BR disassemble (1),
.BR vircon2png (1),
.BR vircon2wav (1)
.SH BUGS
An undocumented
.BI \-o " folder"
option sets the output folder too, as an alternative to the second
argument.
.SH AUTHOR
The Vircon32 ROM unpacker was written by Javier Carracedo
.RI ( Carra ).
This manual page was written by Matthew Haas for the v32c++ project.
